<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
  <title>Client certificate | Sluice console</title>
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{#src}}/console/img/logo.svg{{/src}}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{#src}}/console/css/console.css{{/src}}">
</head>
<body class="cert-page">
<header class="masthead">
  <a class="brand" href="/console">
    <svg class="brand__mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M3 9h9M3 23h9M20 9h9M20 23h9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <path d="M12 9l4 7M12 23l4-7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
      <path d="M2 16h8M22 16h8" fill="none" stroke="var(--water)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="2 3"/>
    </svg>
    <span class="brand__word">sluice</span>
    <span class="brand__sub">console</span>
  </a>
</header>

<main class="cert-page__column">
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="certificates-heading">
    <h1 id="certificates-heading" class="rule-heading">Client certificate</h1>
    {{#clientCertificate}}
    <p class="hint">Issues a key pair signed by <span class="mono">{{caSubject}}</span> for the mTLS control plane; the client presents it via <code>sluice.tls-bundle</code>.</p>
    <form class="cert-form" method="post" action="/console/certificates">
      {{#_csrf}}<input type="hidden" name="{{_csrf.parameterName}}" value="{{_csrf.token}}">{{/_csrf}}
      <div class="cert-form__field">
        <label for="cert-common-name">Common name</label>
        <input id="cert-common-name" name="cn" type="text" required pattern="[A-Za-z0-9._-]+"
               autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="client-1">
        <p class="hint">Free form -- any name that identifies the client; the server does not match on it. Characters outside letters, digits, dot, underscore and hyphen are dropped.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cert-form__field">
        <label for="cert-validity-days">Validity (days)</label>
        <input id="cert-validity-days" name="days" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="365">
      </div>
      <button class="cert-form__submit" type="submit">Issue and download</button>
    </form>
    <p class="hint">The zip is named after the common name and holds three PEM files: <code>&lt;name&gt;.crt.pem</code> (certificate), <code>&lt;name&gt;.key.pem</code> (PKCS#8 key) and <code>ca.crt.pem</code> (trust anchor).</p>
    <p class="hint">On the client, unzip next to the application and point an SSL bundle and the tunnel at them:</p>
    <pre class="cert-example"><code>sluice.server-url=grpcs://sluice.example.com:8001
sluice.token=&lt;token&gt;
sluice.client.id=client-1
sluice.tls-bundle=client-1
spring.ssl.bundle.pem.client-1.keystore.certificate=file:client-1.crt.pem
spring.ssl.bundle.pem.client-1.keystore.private-key=file:client-1.key.pem
spring.ssl.bundle.pem.client-1.truststore.certificate=file:ca.crt.pem

sluice.client.upstream[0].host=app.example.com
sluice.client.upstream[0].target=http://127.0.0.1:8080</code></pre>
    {{/clientCertificate}}
    {{^clientCertificate}}
    <p class="empty">No CA configured. Point <code>sluice.ca-bundle</code> at an SSL bundle holding the issuer key pair to enable issuance.</p>
    {{/clientCertificate}}
  </section>
</main>
</body>
</html>
